## Final Judgement
## Summary

The fact-check reveals that the claim contains multiple false assertions. First, Joe Biden was not the sitting US President on October 18, 2020—he was a presidential candidate who didn't assume office until January 20, 2021. Second, while a laptop associated with Hunter Biden did surface in October 2020 and reportedly contained "nearly 25,000 images," these were described as "sexually explicit selfies and porn" along with personal photos—not images of torture or rape of children. No forensic examination, credible news organization, or independent expert confirmed the existence of images depicting Hunter Biden torturing or raping children under 10 in China. Additionally, Hunter Biden has never been charged, arrested, or convicted of any crime involving child sexual abuse material.

## Missing Information

No further information is needed. The evidence is clear and comprehensive across multiple independent sources.

## Conclusion

The claim is explicitly and clearly refuted by the evidence. Multiple elements of the claim are demonstrably false: Joe Biden was not president at the time, the laptop images were not of child torture or rape, there is no evidence of children under 10 being depicted, and no connection to China was established. No credible source has corroborated any part of the specific allegations about child torture and rape imagery.

`refuted`

